DDA ray grid traversal:
Given point (x,y), direction (dx,dy), cell size c, grid origin x=-radius, 
y=radius (top). Grid indices i = (x + radius)/c, j = (radius - y)/c. Need 
traverse cells. But because y axis inverted, we can transform to grid coords: u 
= (x+radius)/c, v = (radius - y)/c. Direction in u,v: du = dx/c, dv = -dy/c. 
Start at u0, v0. We can step through cells. At each cell, compute distance along
ray to cell. But we need distance d in world metres for ray height. We can 
compute d at cell crossing.

